|name2 = True Kyosaka Nanaho
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''True Kyosaka Nanaho''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Kyosaka Nanaho's main selling point is her versatility as a Long Distance unit and as a slot saver. Her best matchup is against [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal Enemies]], thanks to her Insanely Tough ability, reliable Critical Hits, and very long piercing range to wipe out approaching Metals, although it is still recommended to pair her with other [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critters]] to cover her blind spot. Her potency is further improved by her survivability, being able to survive a lethal strike while sporting a high knockback count. However, it should be noted that almost every common Metal Enemy in the game is an exceptionally aggressive pusher, which may leave her vulnerable should one inevitably breach her blind spot. Because of this, using her with Breakerblast Cannon or Iron Wall is recommended; exceptionally tanky meatshields such as [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern Cat]] or [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]] should also be utilized to prevent enemies from pushing.

Her Zombie Killer should be considered an added bonus on mixed stages like [[Metallic Metaverse]]; her usage against [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie Enemies]] is limited because Zombies will find it easy to burrow into her blind spot after reaching your front line. While it does find use in [[March to Death (Merciless)|March to Death]] with dealing with the various [[Sir Metal Seal|Metal Seals]] and [[Super Metal Hippoe]]s, her damage and health will not suffice for dealing with [[Daboo of the Dead|Daboo]], or the continuously spawning Metal peons in the long term. This makes her only good for the first wave of metal enemies.

Her ability to break [[Barrier]]s, on the other hand, is quite useful due to her piercing range. This myriad of abilities ultimately serves to create one of the most efficient anti-Metal units in the entire game. Due to her immense coverage of enemy types: from [[Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] with Barriers such as [[UltraBaaBaa]] or [[Youcan]]; to Zombie backliners and peons with annoying revive abilities. It grants her immense usage in mixed stages as one of the few critters that can hold their own as a decent DPS for other traits, which is a privilage that most other anti-Metal units are not privy to. Though her damage overall is still less than stellar, and she lacks [[Wave Attack|Wave]] or [[Surge Attack|Surge]] immunities for enemies such as [[Koronium]], she stands as an insanely versatile pick for any stage with even just one bothersome Metal Enemy.

